er":null,"produced_mana":["U"],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land \u2014 Island"}],"fixture_kind":"pinned-original-static-recipient-qualifications","rulings":[{"comment":"Time of Heroes affects any creature you control with a level counter on it, not just levelers. (Of course, it\u2019s pretty hard to get level counters onto a creature that\u2019s not a leveler, but it can be done with copy effects, Fate Transfer, or Quicksilver Elemental, among other possibilities.)","oracle_id":"fcfb96d7-9b3b-4f60-8714-eebe4d9c002b","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Each creature you control with a level counter on it gets just +2/+2, regardless of how many level counters it has. It doesn\u2019t get the bonus for each counter.","oracle_id":"fcfb96d7-9b3b-4f60-8714-eebe4d9c002b","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Earth Surge gives the bonus to each permanent that has both the \"land\" and \"creature\" types. It doesn't turn lands into creatures.","oracle_id":"fb8fae53-3b06-41d8-baa0-638820a4b550","published_at":"2006-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"As long as Arcades Sabboth is untapped and isn\u2019t attacking, it gets +0/+2 from its own third ability.","oracle_id":"8ead94c5-8447-4f20-87ec-efdccde689fc","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like indestructible and the ability granted by Belligerent Sliver, having more than one instance of the ability doesn\u2019t provide any additional benefit.","oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you change the creature type of a Sliver you control so it\u2019s no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures you control.","oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Slivers in this set affect only Sliver creatures you control. They don\u2019t grant bonuses to your opponents\u2019 Slivers. This is the same way Slivers from the Magic 2014 core set worked, while Slivers in earlier sets granted bonuses to all Slivers.","oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Damage dealt to a Sliver with indestructible is still marked on that creature. If it has lethal damage marked on it and it loses indestructible (perhaps because Sliver Hivelord leaves the battlefield), it will be destroyed.","oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A creature\u2019s level is based on how many level counters it has on it, not how many times its level up ability has been activated or has resolved. If a leveler gets level counters due to some other effect (such as Clockspinning) or loses level counters for some reason (such as Vampire Hexmage), its level is changed accordingly.","oracle_id":"0bc2875b-3a5a-4885-86b9-16ab7330ac10","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Effects that modify a leveler\u2019s power or toughness, such as the effects of Giant Growth or Glorious Anthem, will apply to it no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for counters that change the creature\u2019s power or toughness (such as +1/+1 counters) and effects that switch its power and toughness.","oracle_id":"0bc2875b-3a5a-4885-86b9-16ab7330ac10","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If another creature becomes a copy of a leveler, all of the leveler\u2019s printed abilities \u2014 including those represented by level symbols \u2014 are copied. The current characteristics of the leveler, and the number of level counters on it, are not. The abilities, power, and toughness of the copy will be determined based on how many level counters are on the copy.","oracle_id":"0bc2875b-3a5a-4885-86b9-16ab7330ac10","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Effects that set a leveler\u2019s power or toughness to a specific value, including the effects from a level symbol\u2019s ability, apply in timestamp order. The timestamp of each level symbol\u2019s ability is the same as the timestamp of the leveler itself, regardless of when the most recent level counter was put on it.","oracle_id":"0bc2875b-3a5a-4885-86b9-16ab7330ac10","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The abilities a leveler grants to itself don\u2019t overwrite any other abilities it may have. In particular, they don\u2019t overwrite the creature\u2019s level up ability; it always has that.","oracle_id":"0bc2875b-3a5a-4885-86b9-16ab7330ac10","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Any permanent can be targeted by the second ability, not just one with counters on it.","oracle_id":"fcb2a95b-cef0-4b29-8b2b-538f380aff2b","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Vampire Hexmage's ability can't target a permanent card in a zone other than the battlefield, such as a suspended card.","oracle_id":"fcb2a95b-cef0-4b29-8b2b-538f380aff2b","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you Donate an Aura, it stays where it is, but the targeted player now controls it.","oracle_id":"049d1fb2-cce7-40e7-a633-e84cf9782d89","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Dryad Arbor is changed into another basic land type (such as by Sea's Claim), it continues to be a creature and a Dryad.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Although originally printed with a characteristic-defining ability that defined its color, this card now has a color indicator. This color indicator can't be affected by text-changing effects (such as the one created by Crystal Spray), although color-changing effects can still overwrite it.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Dryad Arbor is changed into another basic land type, it continues to be a green Dryad creature.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Due to its color indicator (appearing to the left of its type line), Dryad Arbor is green. Color indicators apply in all zones, not just the battlefield.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Dryad Arbor is played as a land. It doesn't use the stack, it's not a spell, it can't be responded to, it has no mana cost, and it counts as your land play for the turn.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Forest is a land type and Dryad is a creature type.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a Dryad Arbor gains flash, or you have the ability to play Dryad Arbor as though it had flash (due to Teferi, Mage of Zhalfir or Scout's Warning, for example), you can ignore the normal timing rules for when during your turn you can play a land, but not any other restrictions. You can't play Dryad Arbor during another player's turn, and you can't play Dryad Arbor if you don't have any land plays remaining.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"After it becomes a creature, Mishra's Factory will still have all its abilities.","oracle_id":"5963e0ef-e0bc-4611-ad4f-813a4c0eacfb","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A noncreature permanent that becomes a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn't matter how long the permanent has been a creature. Notably, if you turn Mishra's Factory into a creature on the turn it entered the battlefield, you won't be able to then activate its first or last abilities.","oracle_id":"5963e0ef-e0bc-4611-ad4f-813a4c0eacfb","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.","oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not a toggle effect. If you use Twiddle to tap a card and before it takes effect your opponent taps it, Twiddle will not automatically untap the card.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The decision whether or not to tap or untap is made on resolution. This is not a modal spell.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":{"description":"Pinned Oracle/rulings; explicit synthetic basic-land fixture for isolated native decks"}}
